{"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/mixpanelencoding"]}],"identifier":{"interfaceLanguage":"swift","url":"doc:\/\/MixpanelEncoding\/documentation\/MixpanelEncoding"},"kind":"symbol","hierarchy":{"paths":[[]]},"schemaVersion":{"patch":0,"major":0,"minor":3},"sections":[],"abstract":[{"text":"Send records to a Mixpanel project through its track API.","type":"text"}],"metadata":{"externalID":"MixpanelEncoding","modules":[{"name":"MixpanelEncoding"}],"symbolKind":"module","title":"MixpanelEncoding","roleHeading":"Framework","role":"collection"},"topicSections":[{"title":"Sending to Mixpanel","identifiers":["doc:\/\/MixpanelEncoding\/documentation\/MixpanelEncoding\/HTTPDestinations\/HTTPDestination\/mixpanel(projectToken:region:plan:backoff:clock:now:)","doc:\/\/MixpanelEncoding\/documentation\/MixpanelEncoding\/HTTPDestinations\/HTTPDestination\/mixpanel(projectToken:region:plan:transport:backoff:clock:now:)","doc:\/\/MixpanelEncoding\/documentation\/MixpanelEncoding\/MixpanelRegion","doc:\/\/MixpanelEncoding\/documentation\/MixpanelEncoding\/HTTPDestinations\/ExponentialBackoff\/mixpanel","doc:\/\/MixpanelEncoding\/documentation\/MixpanelEncoding\/MixpanelSetupError"],"anchor":"Sending-to-Mixpanel"},{"title":"Encoding batches","identifiers":["doc:\/\/MixpanelEncoding\/documentation\/MixpanelEncoding\/MixpanelBatchEncoder"],"anchor":"Encoding-batches"},{"title":"Records left out","identifiers":["doc:\/\/MixpanelEncoding\/documentation\/MixpanelEncoding\/MixpanelEncodingError"],"anchor":"Records-left-out"}],"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"content","content":[{"text":"Overview","type":"heading","level":2,"anchor":"Overview"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/MixpanelEncoding\/documentation\/MixpanelEncoding\/HTTPDestinations\/HTTPDestination\/mixpanel(projectToken:region:plan:backoff:clock:now:)","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" makes an"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"HTTPDestination"},{"type":"text","text":" (module "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/HTTPDestinations\/documentation\/HTTPDestinations","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":") for your Mixpanel project in one call. It checks"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"the project token, posts to the "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"\/track"},{"type":"text","text":" endpoint of the project’s data residency"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"("},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/MixpanelEncoding\/documentation\/MixpanelEncoding\/MixpanelRegion","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":"), with "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"verbose=1"},{"type":"text","text":", through a "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/MixpanelEncoding\/documentation\/MixpanelEncoding\/MixpanelBatchEncoder","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":", and splits each batch to Mixpanel’s limits"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"("},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/MixpanelEncoding\/documentation\/MixpanelEncoding\/MixpanelBatchEncoder\/batchLimit","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":"): 2,000 events and 2 MB a request. A batch with no record the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"encoder can write, an empty one included, makes no request. It retries no response, a 5xx, 408"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"and 429, waiting "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/MixpanelEncoding\/documentation\/MixpanelEncoding\/HTTPDestinations\/ExponentialBackoff\/mixpanel","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":": Mixpanel’s recommended"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"schedule, 2 s doubling to 60 s. The full jitter on top is Traffluent’s own choice. It drops and"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"reports any other status. The token goes in each event, so no header field is needed, and no"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"trace context is sent. "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"import Traffluent"},{"type":"text","text":" leaves this module out; import it on its own."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The project token is public: Mixpanel’s own apps and web pages ship it. The destination takes"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"nothing else. Never put the project’s secret or a service account’s credentials in an app; they"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"belong to Mixpanel’s import API, for servers. The factory throws "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/MixpanelEncoding\/documentation\/MixpanelEncoding\/MixpanelSetupError","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" for an"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"empty token, and for one with a character other than a letter or digit, which no project token"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"has."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The region has no default. A project’s data resides in the US, the EU or India, and Mixpanel"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"ingests nothing for it from another residency’s endpoint, so you pick the region on purpose."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Each record becomes an event of an anonymous user. Its ","type":"text"},{"code":"distinct_id","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" is the record’s session,","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"from the sessions enricher, also sent as ","type":"text"},{"code":"$device_id","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":"; a record with no session is sent under its","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"own record identifier, with no ","type":"text"},{"code":"$device_id","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":". Under Simplified ID Merge, Mixpanel shows a","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"session’s events under ","type":"text"},{"code":"$device:<session>","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", and a sessionless record’s under its bare record","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"identifier. No ","type":"text"},{"code":"$user_id","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" is sent. Its ","type":"text"},{"code":"$insert_id","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" is the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"record’s identifier, which a redelivered record keeps, and its ","type":"text"},{"code":"time","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" the record’s timestamp in","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"epoch milliseconds. The record’s vendor identifier and trace context aren’t sent. Each event’s","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"ip","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" is ","type":"text"},{"code":"0","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", as is the endpoint’s, so Mixpanel adds no location from the request’s address. The","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"standard context is sent as Mixpanel’s default properties (","type":"text"},{"code":"$app_version_string","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":",","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"$app_build_number","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"code":"$model","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"code":"$wifi","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"code":"$os","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" and ","type":"text"},{"code":"$os_version","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":").","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Mixpanel counts a user per "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"distinct_id"},{"type":"text","text":", so each session is one user in its reports, and so is"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"each record sent without a session. On a Mixpanel plan billed by monthly tracked users, each counts"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"as one."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Properties are read through the event’s schema in the "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"TrackingPlan"},{"type":"text","text":" the encoder is made with. A"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Sensitive"},{"type":"text","text":" value is never sent, whatever the record reveals. A record the encoder can’t write is"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"left out and the rest of the batch is sent: one the plan doesn’t describe, one whose event name"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"starts with "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"$"},{"type":"text","text":", as Mixpanel’s own events’ names do, one with a property Mixpanel reads for itself"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"(a "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"$"},{"type":"text","text":"-prefixed one, "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"token"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"time"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"distinct_id"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"ip"},{"type":"text","text":" or "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"bucket"},{"type":"text","text":"), one of 255 properties or"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"more counting the encoder’s own, one holding an array of 255 elements or more, one whose property"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"nests objects more than 3 deep, one whose event isn’t"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Encodable"},{"type":"text","text":", one holding a value JSON can’t, one whose timestamp is before 1971 or has no"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"epoch-milliseconds form, one tracked more than 119 hours before its batch is encoded or more than"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"an hour after, and one too large for Mixpanel. The destination reports each as"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"HTTPDropReport.skipped(_:)"},{"type":"text","text":", a "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"SkippedRecord"},{"type":"text","text":" whose reason is a "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/MixpanelEncoding\/documentation\/MixpanelEncoding\/MixpanelEncodingError","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":"."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Mixpanel answers 200 even when it finds no valid event in a request. The endpoint asks for"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"verbose=1"},{"type":"text","text":", so the answer’s body says so, "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"{\"status\": 0, \"error\": ...}"},{"type":"text","text":", and the destination"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"drops the request and reports it as "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"HTTPDropReport.rejectedInBody(status:reason:recordIDs:)"},{"type":"text","text":","},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"with Mixpanel’s error as the reason. A "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"status"},{"type":"text","text":" of 1 means only that one event or more was well"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"formed: it doesn’t confirm that the token names a project, so a wrong region, or a token of no"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"project, may be answered 200 with nothing stored. Check the project’s Live View after setting the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"destination up."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Mixpanel’s track API ingests only events from the last 5 days, and answers 200 to an older one"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"while storing nothing. So the destination drops and reports such a record rather than send it."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"The encoder leaves out a record tracked more than 119 hours (5 days less an hour, for clocks that"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"disagree) before its batch is encoded, as"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/MixpanelEncoding\/documentation\/MixpanelEncoding\/MixpanelEncodingError\/timestampOutsideWindow","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":". Each request has a deadline 119 hours after its"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"oldest record was tracked, and a request still being retried when it passes isn’t sent again: it"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"is reported as "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"HTTPDropReport.deadlineExceeded(deadline:recordIDs:)"},{"type":"text","text":". Pass the factory’s "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"now:"},{"type":"text","text":" a"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"clock of your own to test this."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"To send to PostHog or Amplitude, use ","type":"text"},{"code":"PostHogEncoding","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" or ","type":"text"},{"code":"AmplitudeEncoding","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" instead.","type":"text"}]},{"syntax":"swift","code":["import HTTPDestinations","import MixpanelEncoding","import TrackingPlans","","let plan = try TrackingPlan()","let mixpanel = try HTTPDestination.mixpanel(","    projectToken: projectToken,","    region: .us,  \/\/ or .eu or .india, where the project's data resides","    plan: plan)","let tracker = Tracker(enrichers: [.sessions()])","let delivery = tracker.records.batch().deliver(to: mixpanel)"],"type":"codeListing"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The guide "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"https:\/\/tyler-keith-thompson.github.io\/Traffluent\/documentation\/traffluent\/choosingdestinations","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"covers what Mixpanel receives, and why, in more detail."}]}]}],"references":{"doc://MixpanelEncoding/documentation/MixpanelEncoding/HTTPDestinations/HTTPDestination/mixpanel(projectToken:region:plan:backoff:clock:now:)":{"role":"symbol","title":"mixpanel(projectToken:region:plan:backoff:clock:now:)","url":"\/documentation\/mixpanelencoding\/httpdestinations\/httpdestination\/mixpanel(projecttoken:region:plan:backoff:clock:now:)","type":"topic","kind":"symbol","conformance":{"availabilityPrefix":[{"text":"Available when","type":"text"}],"constraints":[{"code":"Transport","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" is ","type":"text"},{"code":"URLSessionTransport","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" and ","type":"text"},{"code":"Encoding","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" is ","type":"text"},{"code":"MixpanelBatchEncoder","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":".","type":"text"}],"conformancePrefix":[{"text":"Conforms when","type":"text"}]},"identifier":"doc:\/\/MixpanelEncoding\/documentation\/MixpanelEncoding\/HTTPDestinations\/HTTPDestination\/mixpanel(projectToken:region:plan:backoff:clock:now:)","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"static"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"keyword","text":"func"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"mixpanel"},{"kind":"text","text":"("},{"kind":"externalParam","text":"projectToken"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:SS","kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"String"},{"kind":"text","text":", "},{"kind":"externalParam","text":"region"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:16MixpanelEncoding0A6RegionO","kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"MixpanelRegion"},{"kind":"text","text":", "},{"kind":"externalParam","text":"plan"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:13TrackingPlans0A4PlanV","kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"TrackingPlan"},{"kind":"text","text":", "},{"kind":"externalParam","text":"backoff"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:16HTTPDestinations18ExponentialBackoffV","kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"ExponentialBackoff"},{"kind":"text","text":", "},{"kind":"externalParam","text":"clock"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"kind":"keyword","text":"some"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:12_Concurrency5ClockP","kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Clock"},{"kind":"text","text":"<"},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:s8DurationV","kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Duration"},{"kind":"text","text":">, "},{"kind":"externalParam","text":"now"},{"kind":"text","text":": () -> "},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:20FoundationEssentials4DateV","kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Date"},{"kind":"text","text":") "},{"kind":"keyword","text":"throws"},{"kind":"text","text":"("},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:16MixpanelEncoding0A10SetupErrorO","kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"MixpanelSetupError"},{"kind":"text","text":") -> "},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:16HTTPDestinations15HTTPDestinationV","kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"HTTPDestination"},{"kind":"text","text":"<"},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:16HTTPDestinations19URLSessionTransportV","kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"URLSessionTransport"},{"kind":"text","text":", "},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:16MixpanelEncoding0A12BatchEncoderV","kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"MixpanelBatchEncoder"},{"kind":"text","text":">"}],"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A destination that sends batches to the Mixpanel project of "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"projectToken"},{"type":"text","text":", whose data"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"resides in "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"region"},{"type":"text","text":", with "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"URLSession.shared"},{"type":"text","text":", retrying a send that fails for now with the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"waits of "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"backoff"},{"type":"text","text":" on "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"clock"},{"type":"text","text":"."}]},"doc://MixpanelEncoding/documentation/MixpanelEncoding/MixpanelBatchEncoder/batchLimit":{"url":"\/documentation\/mixpanelencoding\/mixpanelbatchencoder\/batchlimit","title":"batchLimit","identifier":"doc:\/\/MixpanelEncoding\/documentation\/MixpanelEncoding\/MixpanelBatchEncoder\/batchLimit","kind":"symbol","type":"topic","abstract":[{"text":"Mixpanel’s limits on one request: 2,000 events, 2,000,000 bytes of body, and 999,999 bytes","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"of one event.","type":"text"}],"role":"symbol","fragments":[{"text":"static","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"let","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"batchLimit","kind":"identifier"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"text":"BatchLimit","preciseIdentifier":"s:12PropertyJSON10BatchLimitV","kind":"typeIdentifier"}]},"https://tyler-keith-thompson.github.io/Traffluent/documentation/traffluent/choosingdestinations":{"type":"link","title":"Choosing Destinations","titleInlineContent":[{"text":"Choosing Destinations","type":"text"}],"url":"https:\/\/tyler-keith-thompson.github.io\/Traffluent\/documentation\/traffluent\/choosingdestinations","identifier":"https:\/\/tyler-keith-thompson.github.io\/Traffluent\/documentation\/traffluent\/choosingdestinations"},"doc://MixpanelEncoding/documentation/MixpanelEncoding/MixpanelBatchEncoder":{"url":"\/documentation\/mixpanelencoding\/mixpanelbatchencoder","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"MixpanelBatchEncoder"}],"title":"MixpanelBatchEncoder","identifier":"doc:\/\/MixpanelEncoding\/documentation\/MixpanelEncoding\/MixpanelBatchEncoder","kind":"symbol","type":"topic","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The "},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/HTTPDestinations\/documentation\/HTTPDestinations\/BatchEncoder"},{"type":"text","text":" of Mixpanel’s track API, so an "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"HTTPDestination"},{"type":"text","text":" can send"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"events to a Mixpanel project’s "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"POST \/track"},{"type":"text","text":"."}],"role":"symbol","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"MixpanelBatchEncoder"}]},"doc://MixpanelEncoding/documentation/MixpanelEncoding/MixpanelRegion":{"role":"symbol","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"enum"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"MixpanelRegion"}],"navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"MixpanelRegion"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/MixpanelEncoding\/documentation\/MixpanelEncoding\/MixpanelRegion","title":"MixpanelRegion","type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/mixpanelencoding\/mixpanelregion","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The data residency of a Mixpanel project, which decides the "},{"code":"\/track","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" endpoint its events are"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"posted to."}],"kind":"symbol"},"doc://HTTPDestinations/documentation/HTTPDestinations":{"url":"\/documentation\/httpdestinations","title":"HTTPDestinations","identifier":"doc:\/\/HTTPDestinations\/documentation\/HTTPDestinations","kind":"symbol","type":"topic","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Send each batch of records to an HTTP endpoint, and send it again until it arrives."}],"role":"collection"},"doc://MixpanelEncoding/documentation/MixpanelEncoding/MixpanelSetupError":{"role":"symbol","title":"MixpanelSetupError","url":"\/documentation\/mixpanelencoding\/mixpanelsetuperror","kind":"symbol","type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/MixpanelEncoding\/documentation\/MixpanelEncoding\/MixpanelSetupError","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"MixpanelSetupError"}],"fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"enum"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"MixpanelSetupError"}],"abstract":[{"text":"Why ","type":"text"},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/MixpanelEncoding\/documentation\/MixpanelEncoding\/HTTPDestinations\/HTTPDestination\/mixpanel(projectToken:region:plan:transport:backoff:clock:now:)","isActive":true},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"couldn’t make a destination.","type":"text"}]},"doc://MixpanelEncoding/documentation/MixpanelEncoding/MixpanelEncodingError/timestampOutsideWindow":{"fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"case"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"timestampOutsideWindow"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/MixpanelEncoding\/documentation\/MixpanelEncoding\/MixpanelEncodingError\/timestampOutsideWindow","kind":"symbol","type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/mixpanelencoding\/mixpanelencodingerror\/timestampoutsidewindow","title":"MixpanelEncodingError.timestampOutsideWindow","abstract":[{"text":"The record was tracked more than 119 hours before the batch was encoded or more than an","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"hour after it, or the clock the encoder reads gave a NaN or infinite time. Mixpanel’s track","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"API drops an event more than 5 days old while answering 200, the hour to spare being for a","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"queue on Mixpanel’s side and clocks that disagree, and rejects one more than an hour in the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"future.","type":"text"}],"role":"symbol"},"doc://MixpanelEncoding/documentation/MixpanelEncoding":{"role":"collection","title":"MixpanelEncoding","url":"\/documentation\/mixpanelencoding","kind":"symbol","type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/MixpanelEncoding\/documentation\/MixpanelEncoding","abstract":[{"text":"Send records to a Mixpanel project through its track API.","type":"text"}]},"doc://MixpanelEncoding/documentation/MixpanelEncoding/MixpanelEncodingError":{"title":"MixpanelEncodingError","role":"symbol","kind":"symbol","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"enum"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"MixpanelEncodingError"}],"navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"MixpanelEncodingError"}],"type":"topic","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Why "},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/MixpanelEncoding\/documentation\/MixpanelEncoding\/MixpanelBatchEncoder"},{"type":"text","text":" couldn’t send a record, which it leaves out of the batch’s"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"requests as a "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"SkippedRecord"},{"type":"text","text":", and "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"HTTPDestination"},{"type":"text","text":" reports as a dro